    {
     "fact": "F1",
     "source": "thm-hh-parabolic-minimal-representatives-and-length-additivity",
     "source_section": "Statement",
     "quote": "2. **Intrinsic parabolic presentation.** Let $W_J^\\ast$ be the group presented by the restricted Coxeter matrix $(J,m|_J)$ in the sense of [[def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length]]. The canonical homomorphism $W_J^\\ast\\to W_J$, $s\\mapsto s$, is an isomorphism. Hence $(W_J,J)$ is a Coxeter system, its intrinsic length function $\\ell_J$ agrees with the ambient length $\\ell$ on $W_J$, and $W_J\\cap S=J$. 3. **Minimal coset representatives.** Every left coset $W_J a:=\\{ua:u\\in W_J\\}$ ($a\\in W$, [[def-coset]]) has a unique element $d$ of minimal length; it is characterized by $\\ell(sd)>\\ell(d)$ for all $s\\in J$, and it satisfies $$\\ell(ud)=\\ell(u)+\\ell(d)\\qquad\\text{for all }u\\in W_J .$$ Equivalently, every $w\\in W$ has a unique factorization $w=u\\,d$ with $u\\in W_J$ and $d$ the minimal representative of the left coset $W_J d$, and then $\\ell(w)=\\ell(u)+\\ell(d)$. By inversion ($w\\mapsto w^{-1}$ preserves lengths and interchanges the two coset families $\\{W_Ja\\}$ and $\\{aW_J\\}$), every right coset $aW_J:=\\{au:u\\in W_J\\}$ has a unique minimal element $d$, characterized by $\\ell(ds)>\\ell(d)$ for all $s\\in J$ and satisfying $\\ell(du)=\\ell(d)+\\ell(u)$ for all $u\\in W_J$.",
     "uses": [
      "1.1",
      "1.2",
