     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "step-1-4",
     "claim": "For (iii), multiplying out each deletion and reading the inversion numbers with [F1], [F2] and [F3]: deletion of position $1$, $4$ or $6$ gives $4312$, $4231$ or $3421$, each of length $5$; deletion of position $2$ or $5$ gives $4123$ or $2341$, each of length $3$; and deletion of position $3$ gives $1324$ of length $1$. By [F5] each value equals $w_0\\tau_i$ for the reflection $\\tau_i$ conjugated to $s_i$, and each is strictly below $w_0$. Since $\\ell(w_0)=6$, the cover criterion [F5] says a deletion value is covered by $w_0$ exactly when its length is $5$: this holds for $i=1,4,6$ (the deletion words of length $5$ are reduced, since their length equals the inversion number of their value) and fails for $i=2,5,3$, where the deletion words of length $5$ are not reduced. Finally, the elements of $S_4$ of length $5$ are exactly $4312$, $4231$ and $3421$: a permutation has inversion number $5$ if and only if exactly one of the six pairs $i<j$ satisfies $\\sigma(i)<\\sigma(j)$, and the enumeration of the $24$ permutations confirms that this holds only for those three; hence the covers of $w_0$ are precisely the three elements of length $5$, and no element of length $<5$ can be covered by $w_0$ by [F5].",
